From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:33:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm-cma-simplify-cma_declare_contiguous_multi-fix

fix typo in comment

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: "Mike Rapoport (Microsoft)" <rppt@kernel.org>
---
 mm/cma.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/cma.c b/mm/cma.c
index 23638dfaae667..744a07217fc43 100644
--- a/mm/cma.c
+++ b/mm/cma.c
@@ -485,7 +485,7 @@ static phys_addr_t __init cma_find_free_range(phys_addr_t align,
 	phys_addr_t max = 0;
 	u64 i;
 
-	/* no point searching if the system can't addres above 4G */
+	/* no point searching if the system can't address above 4G */
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PHYS_ADDR_T_64BIT))
 		return 0;
 
